// Shared markdownlint ruleset for the repo family, and this repo's own.
//
// Single source of truth for the Markdown bar every consumer inherits.
// A consuming repo points at this file from its own root rather than
// restating the rules:
//
//   { "extends": "../Common-Automation/.markdownlint.jsonc" }
//
// The path is resolved relative to the extending file, so it holds for
// any repo checked out as a sibling of this one - the same sibling
// assumption the Gradle builds and the pre-commit hooks already make.
//
// Read by editors rather than by CI: the markdownlint VS Code extension
// walks up from the file being linted to the workspace folder root. No
// action in this repo runs it, so nothing here can fail a build.
{
    // Markdown prose takes no column cap. Paragraphs are broken at
    // sentence and clause boundaries (semantic line breaks) so that a
    // GitHub-rendered paragraph reflows while a diff stays legible,
    // which produces lines of no particular length. Tables and long
    // URLs cannot wrap at all.
    //
    // Stated here rather than left implicit. Without a config file the
    // extension turns this rule off by itself, but that default applies
    // only while nothing is customized - so the first repo to set any
    // rule would silently get the 80-column limit back across every
    // file it has.
    "MD013": false,

    // Duplicate headings are a real defect only among siblings. A
    // changelog on Keep a Changelog repeats "Added", "Fixed" and
    // "Public contracts changed" once per version section, which is the
    // format working as intended: each pair has a different version
    // heading as its parent. Checking siblings alone still catches the
    // case worth catching, two identical headings inside one section,
    // where an anchor link silently resolves to the first.
    "MD024": {
        "siblings_only": true
    }
}
